<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-245: A FOLDER'S OWN AUDIBILITY PASS ASKS ABOUT THE ROOT THAT HOLDS IT.

  TWO SITES, ONE DEFECT. `STrack::applyChildTrackAudibility` (what you hear)
  and `STrack::collectChildSumEnvelope` (what the folder's overlay draws) both
  asked the MASTER for the root. They are asserted side by side at stages A
  and B below, because a fix to one and not the other would leave the picture
  and the sound disagreeing — which is the state proposal 39 M3's own
  "the overlay is the exact call the painter makes" rule exists to prevent.

  WHAT IS UNDER TEST. `STrack::applyChildTrackAudibility` is the pass that
  enforces the shared mute/solo rule on a folder lane's NESTED lanes — the
  root mixer's null-the-input-plug trick cannot reach them, so a folder mutes
  their clip entries instead (objects/track inv. 17/17a). It asked
  `splacements::rootContainer()` for the root, which is the MASTER, so for a
  folder living inside an arrangement it answered about a tree that folder is
  not in. QBX-245 makes the root a PARAMETER: the top-down driver
  (SStdMixer::applyAudibility) is the root and passes `this`, and the
  recursion hands the same one down.

  WHY THIS NEEDED A CASE OF ITS OWN, and why the obvious fixture cannot see
  it. Two conditions have to hold at once:

    - THE SCOPE MUST BE `arrangement`. In the `global` default (QBX-256)
      `isLaneAudible` does not consult its `root` argument at all and
      `anySoloInForce` folds over every root, so the argument is INERT and a
      master-rooted read answers exactly what a correct one does. Measured:
      the sabotage that restores the master read changed nothing in any of
      531 other tests.
    - THE FOLDER MUST BE AUDIBLE WHILE ONE OF ITS CHILDREN IS NOT. If the
      folder itself is inaudible the ROOT MIXER has already nulled its plug
      and this pass's answer cannot be heard; if every child is audible there
      is nothing to mute. The only shape that discriminates is a folder that
      is audible BECAUSE it holds a soloed lane, with a second child that is
      not that lane.

  So: `Drums` holds ONE top-level lane, a folder, with two nested lanes of one
  copy each of the same sawtooth. Coherent copies sum exactly, so two play at
  0.1333 and one at 0.06665 — a clean factor of two, and the arrangement is
  heard through an asset placed on a master lane because an arrangement root
  is summed nowhere (proposal 09 D8).

  ON THE MASTER-ROOTED READ every stage below reads 0.1333: `anySoloInForce`
  asks the master, the master holds no solo at all, so `anySolo` is false and
  every clip entry is handed "audible". Stages B and D are the discriminators;
  A, C and F are the controls that stop a build from passing them by muting
  the wrong thing, or everything.

  `mixer/soloScope` IS THE KEY THIS CASE WRITES, so it is RUN_SERIAL and it
  restores `global` (SOpt::def()) at the end — the discipline the three other
  cases that write it already follow, and the one the one-owner-per-key rule
  is actually protecting.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="arrangement_folder_solo_scoped">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <set-option key="mixer/soloScope" value="arrangement"/>
    <assert-mixing-options soloScope="arrangement"/>

    <add-track index="-1"/>                 <!-- master 0: carries the asset -->

    <create-arrangement name="Drums"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>   <!-- becomes the folder -->
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="Drums:1" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="Drums:2" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- Nest both carriers under lane 0. REPARENTED IN REVERSE ORDER: taking
         lane 1 out first would renumber lane 2 to 1 under us, so the second
         call would address the lane that had just moved. -->
    <reparent-track source="Drums:2" destParent="Drums:0" destIndex="-1"/>
    <reparent-track source="Drums:1" destParent="Drums:0" destIndex="-1"/>
    <!-- One lane at Drums' top level now: the folder. Its two children are
         Drums:0,0 and Drums:0,1 and each carries one copy. -->
    <assert-track-count arrangement="Drums" count="1"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="Drums:0,0,0" startTime="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="Drums:0,1,0" startTime="0"/>

    <create-asset container="Drums:" startOffset="0" duration="192000"
                  assetName="DrumsAsset"/>
    <place-asset assetName="DrumsAsset" trackPath="0" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- ===== A: THE CONTROL — two coherent copies ===================== -->
    <render filename="afs_A.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_A.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.1283" maxRms="0.1383"/>
    <!-- AND THE FOLDER-SUM PREVIEW, which is a SECOND site with the same
         defect: STrack::collectChildSumEnvelope asked the master for its root
         too, and it is the exact call the overlay painter makes (proposal 39
         M3). Two children, so twice one child's envelope, tolerance 0. -->
    <assert-envelope mode="childSum" trackPath="Drums:0" start="0"
                     length="192000" width="4" column="1" min="-50" max="50"/>

    <!-- ===== B: THE DISCRIMINATOR ======================================
         The FIRST nested lane is soloed. Its folder stays audible — it holds
         a soloed lane — and the SECOND nested lane must go silent, which is
         this pass's own decision and nobody else's. One copy. -->
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0,0" solo="1"/>
    <render filename="afs_B.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_B.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.0647" maxRms="0.0687"/>
    <!-- The preview follows the ear: ONE child's envelope now, exactly half
         of A's. A master-rooted collect reads anySolo=false and draws both. -->
    <assert-envelope mode="childSum" trackPath="Drums:0" start="0"
                     length="192000" width="4" column="1" min="-25" max="25"/>

    <!-- ===== C: RELEASED, back to the control's own number ============= -->
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0,0" solo="0"/>
    <render filename="afs_C.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_C.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.1283" maxRms="0.1383"/>

    <!-- ===== D: THE OTHER CHILD, for symmetry =========================
         A build that muted a FIXED child would pass B and fail here. -->
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0,1" solo="1"/>
    <render filename="afs_D.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_D.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.0647" maxRms="0.0687"/>

    <!-- ===== E: THE SAME SOLO UNDER `global` ==========================
         Both scopes agree here, which is the point: this case is about WHICH
         ROOT the pass asks about, not about the scope. In `global` the rule
         crosses the placement edge instead and arrives at the same answer. -->
    <set-option key="mixer/soloScope" value="global"/>
    <render filename="afs_E.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_E.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.0647" maxRms="0.0687"/>
    <set-option key="mixer/soloScope" value="arrangement"/>
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0,1" solo="0"/>

    <!-- ===== F: THE FOLDER ITSELF SOLOED =============================
         "Inside a soloed ancestor" — underSoloedAncestor( root, lane ), the
         term that most needs the right root — so BOTH children are heard.
         Two copies again. A build that darkened a soloed folder's whole
         subtree would pass B and D and fail here. -->
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0" solo="1"/>
    <render filename="afs_F.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="afs_F.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.1283" maxRms="0.1383"/>
    <set-track-solo trackPath="Drums:0" solo="0"/>

    <!-- The INI comes back as it was: `global` is SOpt::def(). -->
    <set-option key="mixer/soloScope" value="global"/>
    <assert-mixing-options soloScope="global"/>
  </actions>
</SActionScript>
